unlike other large school districts  across the country that retain their  superintendents often for decades at a  time the clark county school district  the fifth largest in the entire country  has been through quite a few yeah  tonight kirsten joyce takes a closer  look  we've had 12 different superintendents  since the inception of the clark county  school district in 1956 but just in the  past 20 years five different  superintendents have been in power and  several have definitely clashed with the  school board in 2000 mr carlos garcia  served for a five-year period and left  followed by dr walt rolfes who retired  after serving four years dr dwight jones  resigned in 2013  and then the position went to pat  skorkowski who retired in 2018.  dr jesus jarrah has led ccsd since 2018  that is until he became the first ccsd  superintendent to be fired from the  board this week  now right after dr kenny guin served as  superintendent from 1969 to 1978. the  first black superintendent dr claude  perkins took the helm but after clashing  with the school board he was pressured  to resign after just three years dr  robert wentz surf from 1982-1989  dr brian kram took the district's helm  in 1989 serving for nearly 11 years then  retired in 2000.
 

